# Frontend-Backend Integration Standards

This guide outlines the standards and patterns for integrating the Next.js frontend with the Spring Boot backend in the Weiqi.com project.

## Architecture Overview

The application uses a client-server architecture:
- Frontend: Next.js application (TypeScript)
- Backend: Spring Boot application (Java)
- Communication: REST APIs and WebSockets
- Authentication: Supabase Auth with JWT tokens

## API Communication

### API Request Flow

1. Frontend makes authenticated requests using the `fetchWithAuth` utility
2. Next.js API routes proxy requests to the backend
3. Backend validates JWT tokens and processes requests

### Frontend API Utilities

Use the `fetchWithAuth` utility for all API calls:

```typescript
import { fetchWithAuth } from "@/utils/api";

// GET request example
const getData = async () => {
  const response = await fetchWithAuth('/api/endpoint');
  return response.json();
};

// POST request example
const createData = async (data) => {
  const response = await fetchWithAuth('/api/endpoint', {
    method: 'POST',
    body: JSON.stringify(data)
  });
  return response.json();
};
```

### API Endpoint Structure

Backend API endpoints follow REST conventions:

```java
@RestController
@RequestMapping("/api/resource-name")
public class ResourceController {
    // GET collection
    @GetMapping
    public List<Resource> getAll() { ... }
    
    // GET single resource
    @GetMapping("/{id}")
    public Resource getById(@PathVariable String id) { ... }
    
    // POST new resource
    @PostMapping
    public Resource create(@RequestBody ResourceDTO dto) { ... }
    
    // PUT update resource
    @PutMapping("/{id}")
    public Resource update(@PathVariable String id, @RequestBody ResourceDTO dto) { ... }
    
    // DELETE resource
    @DeleteMapping("/{id}")
    public void delete(@PathVariable String id) { ... }
}
```

## WebSocket Integration

### WebSocket Connection

Frontend connects to WebSockets using the WebSocketContext provider:

```tsx
// In _app.tsx or layout.tsx
<WebSocketProvider>
  <App />
</WebSocketProvider>
```

### Using WebSockets in Components

```tsx
import { useWebSocket } from "@/contexts/WebSocketContext";

function GameComponent() {
  const { isConnected, subscribe, send } = useWebSocket();
  
  useEffect(() => {
    if (!isConnected) return;
    
    const subscription = subscribe(`/topic/game/${gameId}`, (data) => {
      // Handle incoming messages
    });
    
    return () => {
      subscription?.unsubscribe();
    };
  }, [isConnected, gameId, subscribe]);
  
  const sendMove = (x, y) => {
    send(`/app/game/move/${gameId}`, { x, y });
  };
  
  return (/* component JSX */);
}
```

### Backend WebSocket Configuration

```java
@Configuration
@EnableWebSocketMessageBroker
public class WebSocketConfig implements WebSocketMessageBrokerConfigurer {
    @Override
    public void registerStompEndpoints(StompEndpointRegistry registry) {
        registry.addEndpoint("/ws")
                .setHandshakeHandler(userInterceptor)
                .setAllowedOriginPatterns("*")
                .withSockJS();
    }

    @Override
    public void configureMessageBroker(MessageBrokerRegistry registry) {
        registry.enableSimpleBroker("/topic", "/queue");
        registry.setUserDestinationPrefix("/user");
        registry.setApplicationDestinationPrefixes("/app");
    }
}
```

### WebSocket Message Handlers

```java
@Controller
public class GameController {
    @MessageMapping("/game.move/{roomId}")
    @SendTo("/topic/game/{roomId}")
    public GameStateResponse handleMove(@DestinationVariable String roomId, 
                                       @Payload MoveMessage message) {
        // Process move and return updated game state
    }
}
```

## Authentication Flow

### Token-Based Authentication

1. Frontend authenticates with Supabase
2. Supabase JWT token is included in all API requests
3. Backend validates the token using the Supabase JWT secret

### Frontend Authentication

```typescript
// Fetch with authentication
const response = await fetchWithAuth('/api/endpoint', {
  method: 'POST',
  body: JSON.stringify(data)
});

// WebSocket connection with token
const socket = new SockJS(`/ws?token=${accessToken}`);
```

### Backend Authentication Filter

```java
