## Data Transfer Objects (DTOs)

### Game-Related DTOs

Frontend and backend should use consistent data structures:

#### Frontend (TypeScript)
```typescript
interface GameRoom {
  roomId: string;
  players: Player[];
  board: StoneColor[][];
  currentPlayer: StoneColor;
  gameStatus: GameStatus;
  moveHistory: Move[];
}
```

#### Backend (Java)
```java
public class GameRoomResponse {
    private String roomId;
    private List<Player> players;
    private List<List<Integer>> board;
    private String currentPlayer;
    private GameStatus gameStatus;
    private List<Move> moveHistory;
}
```

## Error Handling

### API Error Responses

Backend should return consistent error responses:

```java
@ExceptionHandler(Exception.class)
public ResponseEntity<ErrorMessage> handleException(Exception ex) {
    ErrorMessage errorMessage = new ErrorMessage(
        HttpStatus.INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR.value(),
        ex.getMessage()
    );
    return new ResponseEntity<>(errorMessage, HttpStatus.INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR);
}
```

Frontend should handle these errors:

```typescript
try {
  const response = await fetchWithAuth('/api/endpoint');
  if (!response.ok) {
    const error = await response.json();
    throw new Error(error.message);
  }
  return await response.json();
} catch (error) {
  // Handle error
}
```

## Environment Configuration

### API URL Configuration

Configure API URLs in environment variables:

```
# Frontend (.env.local)
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8080
NEXT_PUBLIC_WS_URL=http://localhost:8080/ws

# Backend (application.properties)
server.port=8080
```

### Next.js API Proxy

Configure Next.js to proxy API requests to the backend:

```typescript
// next.config.js
const nextConfig = {
  async rewrites() {
    return [
      {
        source: "/api/:path*",
        destination: "http://backend:8080/api/:path*",
      },
    ];
  },
};
```

## Testing Integration

### Frontend API Mocking

Use MSW (Mock Service Worker) to mock API responses in frontend tests:

```typescript
// src/mocks/handlers.ts
import { rest } from 'msw';

export const handlers = [
  rest.get('/api/endpoint', (req, res, ctx) => {
    return res(ctx.json({ data: 'mocked data' }));
  }),
];
```

### Backend Integration Tests

Write integration tests for API endpoints:

```java
@SpringBootTest(webEnvironment = WebEnvironment.RANDOM_PORT)
public class ApiIntegrationTest {
    @Autowired
    private TestRestTemplate restTemplate;
    
    @Test
    public void testEndpoint() {
        ResponseEntity<Resource> response = restTemplate.getForEntity(
            "/api/endpoint", Resource.class);
        assertEquals(HttpStatus.OK, response.getStatusCode());
    }
}
```

